living passengers and crew- they're built into the cost of the ship. By law, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," are required to have sufficient Escape Pods on board at all times, but military ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," are exempt from this rule and may carry fewer than the normal amount (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gaining Emplacement Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gaining_Emplacement_Points?action=edit&redlink=1"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If a Colossal or larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," is destroyed, any character on board who survives may make a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," check to reach an Escape Pod. On a failed check, the character is stuck in a bit of wreckage that has enough air and heat to keep them alive for about an hour. (Obviously, a character who gets into an Escape Pod prior to a ship's destruction does not need to make a check.) Typical Escape Pods are small, single-use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," providing 1 day of life support for eight Medium creatures plus rations for another week and just enough fuel to reach a nearby planet. Many large ships upgrade their Escape Pods to more capable models.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Small Lifeboats"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["These vessels, which can be installed on ships of Colossal size or larger, provide life support for up to fifteen Medium creatures for up to 1 week, and they have enough fuel to fly across a star system to reach a habitable planet. They include extensive survival gear, including emergency shelters, 1 week of rations, water purifiers, and a small hunting blaster. One bay includes (Cost Modifier)/50 Small Lifeboats, and multiple bays may be installed.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Large Lifeboats"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["These vessels, which can be installed on ships of Colossal (Frigate) size or larger, provide life support for up to 50 Medium creatures for up to 2 months, and they include a Class 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," with enough fuel for a single hyperspace jump (plus a little left over for the ion engines and repulsorlifts to use during landing). Survival gear is similar to that of a Small Lifeboat (see above). One bay includes (Cost Modifier)/100 Large Lifeboats, and multiple bays may be installed.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Untrained)"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Escape Pod Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 10 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 10), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 25; +2 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 40; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"htt